🚀 **Hands-On Networking Lab: Analyzing Network Traffic with Wireshark & Kali Linux!**

Today, I explored network traffic analysis using **Wireshark and Kali Linux**.

🔍 **What I Practiced:**
- Set up a local Python HTTP server.
- Used `curl` to send HTTP requests.
- Captured and analyzed network packets using Wireshark.
- Observed the TCP three-way handshake (SYN, SYN-ACK, ACK).
- Identified HTTP GET requests and successful `200 OK` responses.
- Analyzed TCP connection termination.

💡 **Key Takeaway:**

This hands-on lab helped me understand how TCP connections are established, how HTTP communication works, and how network traffic can be monitored and analyzed using Wireshark.

I'm excited to continue building my practical networking and cybersecurity skills, one lab at a time! 🔐💻

